<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Roofing has a trust problem, and it's not your fault. Enough dodgy operators and door-knockers have made homeowners nervous about who they let up a ladder. That's actually your opportunity: show your real work, look professional and trustworthy in your ads, and you stand out instantly from the cowboys. Trust is the whole game in this trade, and it's exactly what a good ad builds.</p>

      <h2>What the ads bring in</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Roof repairs and storm damage</li>
        <li>Full roof replacements and re-roofs</li>
        <li>Flat roofs and rubber roofing</li>
        <li>Fascias, soffits and guttering</li>
        <li>Ridge, moss removal and roof cleaning</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why real footage wins</h2>
      <p>Homeowners can't see their own roof, and they can't judge a roofer on a stock photo. Real footage of your jobs, the finish, the tidy work, the drone shots of a completed roof, proves you're the real deal and puts their mind at ease. So we use <strong>real footage of your work</strong>, filmed on site or from finished jobs, never stock. In a trade built on trust, seeing is believing.</p>

      <h2>What the funnel asks</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Is it a repair, a replacement, or fascias and gutters?</li>
        <li>What type of property, and roughly how old is the roof?</li>
        <li>Which town or postcode is it in?</li>
        <li>When are they looking to get it done, and the best number to reach them.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>That sorts the homeowners with a real job from the ones after a free look or the cheapest patch-up, so your time goes on proper work.</p>

